WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.447
The strongest idea in the Drive material is that OpenHW deliverables form a stack.

2
00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:07.640
Processor RTL is only the center.

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.230
Verification creates repeatable checks.

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.416
Documentation defines configuration and integration boundaries.

5
00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:18.734
Software and platform material connect the processor to a system.

6
00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:23.317
Repository history, CI, issues, tags, and releases create provenance.

7
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:26.240
Roadmaps and policy coordinate expectations.

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.950
Contents differ by project, so use the stack as a checklist and verify every item in current sources.

